  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759832,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 16 Years Metalvotze: A Commodore 64 Chronicle\n\n**16 Years Metalvotze** plunges players into the bleak, oppressive world of Oceania, sixteen years after the events of *1984*. Winston Smith’s rebellion may have been crushed, but the seeds of dissent haven't vanished. You assume the role of Anya, a young woman working in the Ministry of Truth, who discovers a hidden cache of Winston’s writings – a dangerous spark igniting a flicker of hope.\n\nThis side-scrolling action-adventure for the Commodore 64 blends stealth, puzzle-solving, and tense platforming. Navigate the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police, utilizing Anya’s limited hacking skills to disable surveillance systems and access restricted areas. Collect fragments of Winston’s notes to piece together his story and uncover a clandestine network of rebels planning a desperate act of defiance against the Party.\n\nExpect challenging level design, a haunting chiptune soundtrack reflecting the pervasive atmosphere of fear, and a narrative that explores the enduring power of memory and the human spirit in the face of totalitarian control. Can Anya reignite the flame of rebellion, or will she become another victim of Big Brother?"
    },
